From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 12:18:40 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] [VideoPlayer] Dolby Vision settings in the video settings
 dialog

Add a Dolby Vision group to the in-video settings, shown when the
renderer can send the stream as standard Dolby Vision
(RENDERFEATURE_DOLBYVISION): the output itself, whether the enhancement
layer is rendered, its upscaling filter, the chroma MMR's arithmetic,
the reconstruction's filters and the vendor infoframe. They are part
of CVideoSettings and the default video settings, and apply during
playback: CRendererDRMPRIME reopens the engine's stream with changed
options, restages the connector for another infoframe, or switches
between the tunnel and the decoder's own frames.

Signed-off-by: Bryan Hoban <bryan.hoban@gmail.com>
